  "parentCard": {
    "title": "The family-audience card",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "read-aloud",
    "steps": [
      "Gather everyone: today the family is the audience, and an older sibling, or a grown-up, runs the show. Hand this card to them and take your seats.",
      "Act one: the older sibling or grown-up introduces the star, and they count to 10 for everyone, fingers up or hopping steps, while the audience counts along in a whisper.",
      "Act two: they clap their best pattern, and the whole family claps it back like an echo.",
      "Act three: they tell everyone their favorite sound, and each person answers with one word that starts with it, silly words welcome.",
      "They close by reading Hello Ruby aloud, and the star arrives the way it always does: the star is for showing."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "Does a real audience make them bigger or quieter? Both are fine; just notice which.",
      "What does the older sibling or grown-up notice about them that the other grown-ups missed?",
      "After the show, which act do they want to do again?"
    ]
  }
